  "id": "tax.us.2025.rule.obligation-accrued-interest-subtotal",
  "notes": "Aggregates the accrued-interest amounts the subject paid sellers on recorded 2025 obligation acquisitions, from the scalar companion family that projects them out of the canonical acquisition members. This is the adopted rule that turns ordinary facts about purchases into a tax adjustment class; the person is never asked to state the adjustment. It never infers, calculates, or broadens any neighbouring interest or transaction surface, and it publishes nothing unless the acquisition family's own member validation - including the required association to a reported box-1 item - passes.",
